  "paper": "light-quanta",
  "argument": "arg-lq-wien-integration",
  "title": "Integrate for the entropy density",
  "spoken": "The integrated entropy density is minus density over B frequency times the bracketed logarithm minus one, plus a frequency-dependent constant.",
  "explanation": "Integrating 1/T with respect to the density gives the entropy density up to a constant C(nu) that may depend on frequency. The constant cannot simply be dropped; the next step fixes it by a boundary condition.",
  "review": "draft",
  "notation": "modern-pedagogical",
  "unitSystem": "si",
  "assumptions": [
    "The Wien regime: the density follows A nu cubed times exp(−B nu / T).",
    "Entropy density and energy density are compared at one frequency.",
    "These are modern teaching equations in SI notation; the paper writes L for c, R/N for Boltzmann's constant, and β for B."
  ],
